# Six hundred dates, times, skeletons and relative times written by ICU 79.1
# (CLDR 49), the reference this package is held to: each line one of the
# commands of the oracle kept in the round's scratch folder
# (`.claude/worktrees/rebel-scratch/i18n/oracle/`) and what ICU answered,
# separated by tabs. `date` is a locale, a date style, a time style (either
# `none`), milliseconds since 1970 and a zone; `skeleton` a locale and a
# skeleton, answered by its pattern; `relative` a locale, an amount, a unit,
# a width and whether the number is always written; `dpattern` a locale, a
# pattern, milliseconds and a zone. Drawn at random (seed 13) on 2026-11-19
# from 10,914 cases over every locale both CLDR 49 and ICU carry, ICU asked
# for the Gregorian calendar, and only from the cases this package answers
# as ICU does: the 29 it answers otherwise are named in the ledger. Only a
# test build reads the cases.

use i18n
use i18n/dates/internal/date_data
use i18n/dates/internal/date_format
use i18n/dates/internal/relative
use i18n/dates/internal/skeletons
use numbers
use strings
use time

# The cases.
